4 years to finish and he gets $50,000 in loans per year.  So this means that his total amount of loans is 4 years * 50,000 / year = 200,000. He lost a job that paid 25,000 a year for 4 years, and that is 4 * 25,000 = 100,000. Therefore, he needs to earn back 200,000 + 100,000 = 300,000.  His salary before college was 25,000 a year.  Since his college degree tripled his income, his new salary is 25,000 * 3 = 75,000 a year.  Therefore, to earn 300,000 dollars, it will take 300,000 / 75,000 = 4 years.

Therefore, the number of years it would take to earn back the money is 4.
\boxed{4}

